des. Each generation introduces groundbreaking features, from powerful engines to advanced comfort amenities. As we witness the progression from classic models to todays state-of-the-art technology, it is clear that Mercedes-Benz consistently leads in merging opulence with cutting-edge automotive technology. Drivers looking for eco-friendly options will appreciate S-Class variants like the plug-in hybrid, showcasing Mercedes-Benzs commitment to sustainable luxury driving experiences without compromising elegance or power. Model nomenclature Transitioning from the historical context of the S-Class, we delve into the model nomenclature that defines the prestigious line-up of Mercedes-Benz luxury vehicles. The Mercedes-Benz S-Class boasts various models, including the iconic S-Class Saloon, the elegant S-Class Coupe, and the opulent Mercedes-Maybach S-Class. These high-end vehicles offer top-of-the-line comfort and advanced safety features that cater to discerning car enthusiasts seeking unparalleled luxury and automotive innovation. The model nomenclature for these premium saloons reflects their status as benchmark-setting automobiles in design, comfort, and cutting-edge technology. With expressive design language and state-of-the-art safety features integrated seamlessly into each variant, the S-Class range continues to set new standards for luxury carsa testament to Mercedes-Benzs commitment to delivering innovative automotive excellence. Predecessor models Transitioning from the model nomenclature, now lets look at the predecessor models of the Mercedes-Benz S-Class: The W108 and W109 series were the predecessors to the S-Class line, marking a shift towards luxury in 1965. The W116 was another successful predecessor, introducing several safety features like crumple zones and anti-lock brakes. The W126 followed with innovations such as airbags and traction control, setting new comfort and safety technology standards. Continuing the legacy, the W140 featured advanced technology, including double-glazed windows and an infrared remote control system. The W220 series further e', 'images': [], 'rank': 1}, {'url': 'https://www.caranddriver.com/mercedes-benz/s-class', 'content': \"2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class Review, Pricing, and Specs Search Cars By Category Expert Reviews Car Buying Guide Shopping Tools and Advice Car Buying Service Stories and Features News Expert-Tested Gear New Cars Follow Podcast Videos Subscribe to the Magazine About Us Newsletter Privacy Notice Terms Of Use Skip to Content Research Cars Expert Reviews Shopping Tools WHATS MY CAR WORTH? Expert-Tested Gear News + Stories Maintenance Follow Car and Driver Subscribe to the magazine About Us Contact Us Global Nav Search Subscribe sign in Research Cars Expert Reviews Shopping Tools WHATS MY CAR WORTH? Expert-Tested Gear News + Stories Maintenance Home Mercedes-Benz S-class 2025 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 2019 2018 2017 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class 9.5 / 10 C/D RATING Jessica Lynn Walker | Car and Driver Jessica Lynn Walker | Car and Driver Jessica Lynn Walker | Car and Driver Jessica Lynn Walker | Car and Driver View Photos Jessica Lynn Walker | Car and Driver MSRP $118,900$129,750 Car and Driver Accolades What's this? Editors' Choice HIGHS Sophisticated and elegant inside and out, remarkably quick for its size, refined ride. LOWS Overwhelming amount touchscreen controls, adaptive cruise and hands-free mode can get agitated, 3-D gauge cluster is a swing and miss. VERDICT Not only the flagship of the brand, the S-class also serves as the de facto flagship of luxury sedans in general. Specs See all specs EPA MPG 51 Combined Seating 5 Seats Cargo Capacity 813 Cubic Feet Powertrain Gas Drivetrain All-Wheel Drive Limited Warranty 4 Years/50,000 Miles By Andrew Wendler Overview Long the choice for buyers seeking solid, unaffable deportment and a distinguished presence, the Mercedes-Benz S-class has become synonymous with power and wealth. Its six-figure starting price certainly plays a part, but it wouldn't have stayed on top for so long without the class-leading ride and comfort, upscale furnishings, and smooth and muscular powertrains that define it. The latter comes in the form of either a 442-hp turbocharged straight-six, a 496-hp twin-turbo V-8, or a plug-in hybrid that pairs the turbo six with an electric motor. The ride and handling benefit from a standard air-spring suspension, and heated and ventilated massaging front seats coddle the occupants. Well-equipped as standard, there's also a long list of optional hides, woods, and colors to personalize the S-class to your taste. If there is an area of contention, it's the sheer number of screens and their almost overwhelming amount of controls and features. Still, while many rivals including the Audi A8 , BMW 7-series , and Genesis G90 have made inroads onto the big Benz's turf, for now at least, it remains the king of full-size luxury sedans. As one of our favorites in its segment, the Mercedes-Benz S-class has also earned a spot on our Editors Choice list for 2025 . Where This Vehicle Ranks #1 in Best Full-Size Luxury Cars 1 Mercedes-Benz S-class STARTING AT: $118,900 2 Genesis G90 STARTING AT: $91,195 3 BMW 7-series STARTING AT: $98,475 4 Mercedes-AMG S-Class STARTING AT: $187,350 5 Audi A8 STARTING AT: $93,295 6 Audi S8 STARTING AT: $126,595 New! Compare the 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-class with the top vehicles in this segment with our new compare tool. Compare the top cars What's New for 2025? Mild updates arrive for 2025, including a center airbag and a standard digital key. New Verde Silver and Sonoran Brown exterior paint hues that fill in for the departing Mojave Silver and Onyx Black. The four-zone climate control, previously available only as part of a package, is now a standalone option; similarly, AMG Line trim is now a standalone package that can be added to the Luxury and Executive trims. Those looking for an even mightier, performance-focused model can check out the AMG S-class . And for those with money to burn, there's the Mercedes-Maybach S-class (both reviewed separately). Pricing and Which One to Buy The price of the 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-class starts at $118,900 and goes up to\", 'images': [], 'rank': 2}, {'url': 'https://mercedes-specs.com/s-class/2021-present/specs/', 'content': 'Mercedes-Benz Mercedes S-Class 2021-present Specifications | Mercedes-Benz Specs Home Models Mercedes A-Class Mercedes B-Class Mercedes C-Class Mercedes CLA Mercedes CLK Mercedes CLS Mercedes E-Class Mercedes G-Class Mercedes GLA Mercedes GLB Mercedes GLC Mercedes GLE Mercedes GLK Mercedes GLS Mercedes M-Class Mercedes R-Class Mercedes S-Class Mercedes SL Mercedes SLC Mercedes SLK Mercedes SLS Mercedes Sprinter Mercedes Vito About Contact More Makes Acura Audi BMW Buick Cadillac Chevrolet Chrysler Dodge Ferrari Ford GMC Honda Hyundai Infiniti Jaguar Jeep Kia Land Rover Lexus Lincoln Maserati Mazda Mercedes-Benz Mitsubishi Nissan Pontiac Porsche RAM Subaru Tesla Toyota Volkswagen Volvo Home Models Mercedes A-Class Mercedes B-Class Mercedes C-Class Mercedes CLA Mercedes CLK Mercedes CLS Mercedes E-Class Mercedes G-Class Mercedes GLA Mercedes GLB Mercedes GLC Mercedes GLE Mercedes GLK Mercedes GLS Mercedes M-Class Mercedes R-Class Mercedes S-Class Mercedes SL Mercedes SLC Mercedes SLK Mercedes SLS Mercedes Sprinter Mercedes Vito About Contact Home Mercedes-Benz Mercedes S-Class 2021-present Specifications Navigation S-CLASS 2021-PRESENT 2021-PRESENT specs Mercedes-Benz Mercedes S-Class 2021-present Mercedes-Benz Mercedes S-Class 2021-present Specifications Complete technical specifications and performance data for the Mercedes-Benz Mercedes S-Class 2021-present. Includes detailed engine specifications, dimensions, safety features, and more. Quick Navigation Engine Transmission Dimensions Chassis Performance Show More (3) Updated Jan 29, 2025 Engine Transmission Dimensions Chassis Performance Safety Technology FAQ Engine Specifications Engine Type Inline-